 {'idx': 50, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'The Forests and Forest Flora of The Colony of the Cape of Good Hope The Forests and Forest Flora of The Colony of the Cape of Good Hope, is a botanical reference book written and illustrated by Thomas Robertson Sim, and published in 1907 by Taylor & Henderson of Aberdeen. At the time he was the Conservator of Forests of Natal, and had been the District Forest Officer in King William\'s Town, bringing a wealth of experience to the creation of this monumental work. Sim had previously written a great many books such as "Handbook of Kaffrarian Ferns", "The Ferns', 'title': 'The Forests and Forest Flora of The Colony of the Cape of Good Hope'}
