 {'idx': 66, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'Hope\'s south is the Bishop River, a tributary of the Southgate River, beyond which is Mount Raleigh. West of the pass between the Southgate River and Chilko Lake, and north of the Homathko Icefield, is a ridge crowned by Mount Queen Bess. Its name is not directly from the Cape of Good Hope but rather from a ship named for it, the armoured cruiser HMS "Good Hope" which sank off the coast of Chile in the Battle of Coronel, November 1, 1914. Other summits within the same massif also carry ship names from World War I, such as "Glasgow" and', 'title': 'Mount Good Hope'}
