 {'idx': 19, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'Ministry of Economy (Spain) The Ministry of Economy and Business () is the ministerial department of the Spanish government with competences over economic affairs, telecommunications, information society, business and competetiveness. When Mariano Rajoy was elected as the Prime Minister, he divided the ministry into two and appointed Luis de Guindos as the Minister of Economy and Competitiveness of Spain and Cristóbal Montoro as the Minister of the Treasury and Public Function. In 2018, De Guindos left the government to become Vice President of the ECB and Prime Minister Rajoy appointed Román Escolano as new Minister of Economy. The Ministry of', 'title': 'Ministry of Economy (Spain)'}
