 {'idx': 7, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'of the impacted tooth is level or nearly level with the occlusal plane and the cervical line of the adjacent second molar. Impacted wisdom teeth without a communication to the mouth, that have no pathology associated with the tooth and have not caused tooth resorption on the blocking tooth, rarely have symptoms. In fact, only 12% of impacted wisdom teeth are associated with pathology. When wisdom teeth communicate with the mouth, the most common symptom is localized pain, swelling and bleeding of the tissue overlying the tooth. This tissue is called the operculum and the disorder called pericoronitis which means', 'title': 'Impacted wisdom teeth'}
