 {'idx': 5, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'became the trend as they were often removed by the loved ones to be kept as mementos of the deceased. This practice peaked in the late 19th century. In the UK and Australia coffin name plates are legally required (whether for burial and cremation) as a means of identifying the deceased. Coffin plate Coffin plates are decorative adornments attached to a coffin that can contain various inscriptions like the name and death date of the deceased or a simple terms of endearment. They are usually made of a soft metal like lead, pewter, silver, brass, copper or tin. The different', 'title': 'Coffin plate'}]

[{'idx': 0, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'the fight. Several songs were written and released about the fight. For example: The Rumble in the Jungle The Rumble in the Jungle was a historic boxing event in Kinshasa, Zaire (now Democratic Republic of the Congo) on October 30, 1974 (at 4:00 am). Held at the 20th of May Stadium (now the Stade Tata Raphaël), it pitted the undefeated world heavyweight champion George Foreman against challenger Muhammad Ali, a former heavyweight champion; the attendance was 60,000. Ali won by knockout, putting Foreman down just before the end of the eighth round. It has been called "arguably the greatest sporting', 'title': 'The Rumble in the Jungle'}
