 {'idx': 11, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Confidential" he had always wanted to be on the show: "One of my ambitions since the \'60s has been to take part in a "Doctor Who". The other one is "Coronation Street". So I\'ve cracked "Doctor Who" now. I\'m still waiting for "Corrie"." In 2004, Jacobi starred in Friedrich Schiller\'s "Don Carlos" at the Crucible Theatre in Sheffield, in an acclaimed production, which transferred to the Gielgud Theatre in London in January 2005. The London production of "Don Carlos" gathered rave reviews. Also in 2004, he starred as Lord Teddy Thursby in the first of the four-part BBC series "The', 'title': 'Derek Jacobi'}
