 {'idx': 20, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'Riobamba (nightclub) Riobamba was a New York City nightclub. Operating from 1942 to 1944, it was closely associated with singer Frank Sinatra, who made his solo nightclub debut there in 1943. The club was located on East 57th Street near Third Avenue in Manhattan. The Riobamba was owned by American Mafia boss Louis "Lepke" Buchalter. While Buchalter was awaiting execution on death row, his wife ran the club. From 1942 to 1944 the club was managed by Linton D. Weil and Arthur Jawitz. There was a claim that the Duke of York owned the real estate where the club was', 'title': 'Riobamba (nightclub)'}
