 {'idx': 4, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Melton Football Club The Melton Football Netball Club, nicknamed The Bloods, is an Australian Rules Football club playing in the Ballarat Football League. The club is based in the Victorian town of Melton. Melton Football Club was formed in 1879 when it was known as the "Bloods", playing in the Melton and Bacchus Marsh District Football League where the club was successful winning twelve premierships between 1913 and 1963. Melton moved into the Riddell District Football League in 1973. Upon entering the Riddell League in 1973 Melton won the premiership in its first year. With the depth of football standard', 'title': 'Melton Football Club'}
