 {'idx': 7, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'The Boy Who Lost His Face The Boy Who Lost His Face () is a novel by Louis Sachar. The story focuses on a group of young boys. One of them (David), joining in with the \'cool crew\', helps to steal an old woman\'s cane. When she finds them, she cries out, "Your Doppelgänger will regurgitate on your soul!" meaning that his ghostly double would puke on his soul, according to a translation by David. Following this, the protagonist finds himself repeatedly experiencing the same misfortunes he passed on to the old woman. Themes of the occult, youthful sexuality, and', 'title': 'The Boy Who Lost His Face'}
