 {'idx': 3, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'The Round Table (book) The Round Table is a collection of essays by William Hazlitt and Leigh Hunt published in 1817. Hazlitt contributed 40 essays, while Hunt submitted 12. The content of "The Round Table" was mostly taken from Hunt and Hazlitt\'s contributions to "The Examiner", a newspaper which Hunt edited. The material for the first volume was sent to the printer as a collection of newspaper cuttings. The process of publishing the collection had begun in late 1815, but much of the following year was lost to delays caused by its Edinburgh-based publisher, Archibald Constable, who doubted that a', 'title': 'The Round Table (book)'}
