 {'idx': 64, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'The Diving Bell and the Butterfly The Diving Bell and the Butterfly (original French title: "Le Scaphandre et le Papillon") is a memoir by journalist Jean-Dominique Bauby. It describes what his life is like after suffering a massive stroke that left him with locked-in syndrome. It also details what his life was like before the stroke. The French edition of the book was published on March 7, 1997. It received excellent reviews, sold the first 25,000 copies on the day of publication, reaching 150,000 in a week. It went on to become a number one bestseller across Europe. Its total', 'title': 'The Diving Bell and the Butterfly'}
