 {'idx': 80, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'hyphen is only used when writing translated foreign names with hyphens. Otherwise, it is not used in Chinese and omitted when translating compound words. Several punctuation marks have ranges of use that differ from the way they are used in English, though some functions may overlap. Chinese punctuation Chinese punctuation uses a different set of punctuation marks from European languages, although the concept of modern standard punctuation was adapted in the written language during the 20th century from Western punctuation marks. Before that, the concept of punctuation in Chinese literature existed mainly in the form of Judou (), a system', 'title': 'Chinese punctuation'}
