 {'idx': 27, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'Lights Out" (2004) and "Live at Reading" (2009). Throughout his tenure with Scream and Nirvana, Grohl worked on crafting material of his own. Using the pseudonym Late!, Grohl released the album "Pocketwatch" (1992), on which he performed all instruments and vocals. This recording method was adopted three years later with "Foo Fighters" (1995), another album performed entirely by Grohl. After acquiring band members to help support the release, Foo Fighters quickly transformed into a group fronted by Grohl. The band has gone on to release a total of eight studio albums and three EPs to date, in addition to the', 'title': 'Dave Grohl discography'}
