 {'idx': 15, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': "to the title and estates, was unmarried and appointed a lord commissioner of the admiralty in 1714, the implied statement that the family was dependent on Basil is curious. The petition, however, was successful, and a pension of £50 a year was granted to each of the six daughters. Beaumont's portrait, by Michael Dahl, is in the Painted Hall at Greenwich, to which it was presented by King George IV; it is that of a comely young man. These references are found in the DNB article referred to above. Basil Beaumont Basil Beaumont (born 1669 died 1703), rear-admiral, was the", 'title': 'Basil Beaumont'}
