[{'idx': 0, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': "Andrew Wiles Sir Andrew John Wiles (born 11 April 1953) is a British mathematician and a Royal Society Research Professor at the University of Oxford, specialising in number theory. He is best known for proving Fermat's Last Theorem, for which he was awarded the 2016 Abel Prize and the 2017 Copley Medal by the Royal Society. He was appointed Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire in 2000, and in 2018 was appointed as the first Regius Professor of Mathematics at Oxford. Wiles was born on 11 April 1953 in Cambridge, England, the son of Maurice Frank Wiles", 'title': 'Andrew Wiles'}
