 {'idx': 4, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': '59th British Academy Film Awards The 59th British Academy Film Awards, given by the British Academy of Film and Television Arts, took place on 19 February 2006 and honoured the best films of 2005. "Brokeback Mountain" won Best Film, Best Director for Ang Lee, Best Supporting Actor for Jake Gyllenhaal, and Best Adapted Screenplay. Philip Seymour Hoffman won Best Actor for "Capote" and Reese Witherspoon won Best Actress for "Walk the Line". "The Constant Gardener" had the most nominations with 10, but only received one award; Claire Simpson for Best Editing. "", directed by Nick Park and Steve Box, was', 'title': '59th British Academy Film Awards'}
