 {'idx': 5, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Church of St. James the Greater, Sokolniki The Church of St. James the Greater Apostle is a parish in Sokolniki, Września County, Poland, built in the thirteenth century. Its consecration took place in 1416. The current church, constructed in neo-baroque style, was built 1926 and consecrated by August Hlond on 28 August 1932. It is one of 10 parishes within the deanery. On 6 September 2009, the Board of Greater Poland approved the list of operations for the Rural Development Programme for the years 2007 to 2013. The district thus received a grant to repair the church roof. Parish registers:', 'title': 'Church of St. James the Greater, Sokolniki'}]

