 {'idx': 4, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'manuscripts of the Lancelot-Grail are available online at the following locations: The Bibliothèque Nationale de France "Gallica" website lists 10 Lancelot-Grail manuscripts of this work and others containing Arthurian texts, with links to each manuscript. Other manuscripts with images online are: Two British Library manuscripts are fully digitised: For other manuscripts in the British Library collections, descriptions and images are available in the Catalogue of Illuminated Manuscripts: Lancelot-Grail The Lancelot-Grail, also known as the Prose "Lancelot", the Vulgate Cycle, or the Pseudo-Map Cycle, is a major source of Arthurian legend written in French. It is a series of prose volumes', 'title': 'Lancelot-Grail'}]

