 {'idx': 23, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'saying anything and Lennon did not turn around. Chapman remained at the scene and appeared to be reading "The Catcher in the Rye" when the NYPD officers arrived and arrested him without incident. The first responders recognized Lennon\'s wounds were severe and decided not to wait for an ambulance. They rushed the mortally wounded musician to Roosevelt Hospital in a squad car, but nothing could be done to save him. Lennon was pronounced dead by Dr. Stephan Lynn at 11:07 p.m. In his statement to police three hours later, Chapman stated, "I\'m sure the big part of me is Holden', 'title': 'Mark David Chapman'}
