 {'idx': 16, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'Castle of Miranda de Ebro The Castle of Miranda de Ebro is a mediaeval fortification located in Miranda de Ebro, Spain. The castle of Miranda de Ebro is located on Picota hill, in the heart of the old helmet of the city. It is positioned about 500 metres above sea level and offers great views of the city and the mountains that surround it. The origins of the castle of Miranda de Ebro date from 15 October 1358, when Tello of Castille asked the bishopric of Calahorra for the land to construct a castle at the top of the hill', 'title': 'Castle of Miranda de Ebro'}
