 {'idx': 23, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': "Swimming at the 2000 Summer Olympics – Women's 200 metre individual medley The women's 200 metre individual medley event at the 2000 Summer Olympics took place on 18–19 September at the Sydney International Aquatic Centre in Sydney, Australia. Yana Klochkova, Ukraine's swimming pride and three-time European champion, became the fourth swimmer in Olympic history to strike a medley double, since Claudia Kolb did so in 1968, Tracy Caulkins in 1984, and Michelle Smith in 1996. Leading from start to finish, she established a sterling time of 2:10.68 to cut off Lin Li's eight-year Olympic record by a comfortable margin of", 'title': "Swimming at the 2000 Summer Olympics – Women's 200 metre individual medley"}
