 {'idx': 16, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'Vangelis Angelou Evangelos "Vangelis" Angelou (alternate spelling: Vaggelis Aggelou) (; born November 11, 1962 in Chalkida, Greece), is a Greek retired professional basketball player and current professional basketball coach. At 6\'2 " (1.90 m) in height, Angelou played at the point guard position. Angelou began playing basketball with the youth teams of AGE Chalkida. In his pro playing career, Angelou played with Apollon Patras, Olympiacos, Panionios, and Iraklis. He scored 1,782 points in 254 games played in the Greek League. Angelou began his coaching career with AGE Chalkida from 1996–2002, where he led the club from the lower categories of', 'title': 'Vangelis Angelou'}
